fluxecho.module.weather_station=Weather Station
tile.fluxecho.module_core.weather_station.name=Weather Station Core
fluxecho.weather_station.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's weather station§r\nAn instrument hut on a floating platform over the gate and a weather mast whose vanes turn under a slowly churning cloud\nIts four weather consoles keep the team's samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.weather_station.structure=§bThe Weather Station: a floating platform 21×21 and 14 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on the sky ring over the gate (S0) once the Weather Station is researched (phase IV) and the dome generator's pod floats: the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start. The job also lays the catwalk from the pod and opens the pod's door to it\n· A platform of Floating Foundation level with the pod's floor, railed round but for the catwalk's mouth; an instrument hut at the front (walls 4 high, the kit portal, a back door), the weather mast behind it (Frame Pillars, a Flux Conduit and a Crystal Seat 13 high; they give way to rendered vanes and a cloud once it forms) and two vane pylons at the back\n· 4 units, 4 samples: four weather consoles round the mast (a Console Stand and a Sample Socket each); right-click any part of one holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the station\n· The core in the hut's portal between its two doors, two blocks above the deck, facing the pod\n· Made of Floating Foundation and frame parts, Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, rails, posts and Sample Sockets (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
